@startuml
title TASK-260712-3d0zgu - Callback, Policy and Receipt Regression States

hide empty description

state "Opaque callback" as Callback {
  [*] --> pending
  pending --> applied : authorized mutation commits
  pending --> confirmation : interrupt unavailable
  confirmation --> applied : explicit fallback commits
  pending --> too_late : playback start committed first
  confirmation --> too_late : default starts while pending
  pending --> expired : timeout / malformed / wrong message
  pending --> forbidden : wrong actor / orbit / role
  applied --> already_applied : duplicate token or query
  applied --> [*]
  too_late --> [*]
  expired --> [*]
  forbidden --> [*]
  already_applied --> [*]
}

state "Target policy outcome" as Policy {
  [*] --> eligible
  eligible --> blocked : actor block before orbit block
  eligible --> missed_dnd : local/orbit effective DND
  eligible --> missed_offline : offline after policy checks
  eligible --> accepted
  accepted --> cancelling : DND/block/delete during playback
  cancelling --> cancelled : exact fade-stop reason
}

state "Public projection" as Projection {
  [*] --> visible
  visible --> redacted : viewer does not own exact reason
  visible --> actionable : current authority rechecked
  visible --> stale : presence timeout sanitizes runtime state
}

note bottom of Callback
  Replacement uses current target policy state.
end note

note bottom of Policy
  Exact receipts flow to the public projection with ownership redaction.
end note

note bottom
  Tests cover every transition with deterministic clocks and transactions.
  No microphone, process, device, raw Telegram or raw actor identifier
  is permitted in the public history/presence projection.
end note

@enduml
